Modifications: GPUI is used from https://github.com/biw/zed (branch
electron-gpui-embedded-cross-platform), which adds embedded initialization
for macOS, Windows and Linux so the host owns the application event loop,
Windows WARP fallback, and Windows/X11 always-on-top support.

Windows font rendering uses unmodified dwrote DirectWrite bindings
(https://crates.io/crates/dwrote), licensed under MPL-2.0. Source and the
Mozilla Public License are included in the published crate distribution.

Hot patching uses Subsecond (https://github.com/DioxusLabs/dioxus), Copyright
Dioxus Labs, licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. crates/electron-gpui-hotpatch
adapts code from the Dioxus CLI's hot-patching engine
(packages/cli/src/build/patch.rs), used under the MIT license.
